node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.vite

# Capacitor's generated Android project keeps its build output out of the tree.
android/app/build
android/build
android/.gradle
android/app/src/main/assets/public
android/local.properties
*.keystore
keystore.properties

.DS_Store
*.log

# Per-worktree agent state: role, handoff note, and the worktrees themselves.
.claude/role
.claude/handoff.md
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Coordination state: ADR numbers claimed across branches and worktrees.
.claude/adr-claims

# Nothing writes this any more (announce reads branch state directly now),
# but a stale copy from before that change can still be lying around in a
# checkout, and un-ignoring it once already let one get swept into an
# unrelated commit by git add -A. Kept ignored so that cannot happen twice.
.claude/announced

# Per-worktree efficiency instrument: timing and (self-reported, usually
# absent) token counts for session starts and commits. Local to the
# checkout that wrote it, same as the clock file beside it — nobody else's
# stats are this worktree's to read, and a shared file several roles wrote
# to would be the merge conflict the protocol's own files already avoid.
.claude/stats.jsonl
.claude/.stats_clock

# Scratch results from tools/report-facts.sh --run, if ever written here.
.report-tests.json

# Internal fleet working notes: sweep reports and process post-mortems.
# Untracked deliberately, the same reason `.claude/adr-claims` is — except
# that this one is about audience rather than coordination. The repository
# is public; these are candid internal writing, and the user asked for them
# to stay out of the published tree. They are still written, still read, and
# still referred to by path. They are simply not pushed.
docs/findings/
docs/process/

# Per-worktree session telemetry, written by the fleet tooling about the
# session reading it. Untracked for the same reason `node_modules` is — it
# is runtime state of this checkout, not of the project — and ignored
# rather than merely uncommitted because the commit guard fires on
# anything untracked. A guard that fires on files nobody may commit is how
# a guard comes to be scrolled past, and this one would fire at every idle
# for every role.
.claude/stats.jsonl
.claude/.stats_clock

# Fetched recordings for the capture tests. See tools/fetch-test-audio.sh —
# they are 4-6 MiB each and are a build-time input, never shipped.
fixtures/

# The recordings a pack is built FROM are tens of megabytes and are fetched
# by `tools/build-instrument-pack.mjs` into `fixtures/`, which is ignored
# above. The packs themselves are committed, and the first version of this
# rule ignored them too — which was wrong in a way nothing in the suite
# could see.
#
# A pack is only ever loaded over HTTP, so an ignored one is simply absent
# everywhere except the checkout that built it: every other worktree, a
# fresh clone, CI and the deployed site served the SPA fallback for it and
# the app quietly played the synthesised voice instead. It is exactly the
# failure synthesis-as-a-floor is designed to absorb, which is why it was
# silent — no error, no console warning, just nobody ever hearing a
# recording. Found by the user role, from the built app, after main had
# "verified" it against the one working tree where the files happened to
# exist.
#
# 1.5 MB for five instruments, content-addressed and immutable, is not the
# recording corpus the argument above is about. The corpus is the 60 MB of
# source WAVs, and those stay out.
